5.198.m:
The king said:
Please tell me this reason also out of your favour, O brahmin;
you have knowledge of the world, both immobile and mobile.

He grew rapidly like the moon in the bright fortnight,
praised by all people, possessed of a handsome form;
seeing his family, he continually experienced the highest detachment.

5.204.m:
Viṣṇu said:
Knowing this, O thousand-eyed one, carry out my word,
if those who were slain in the forefront of battle are dear to you,

5.205.m:
Some lived crushing food with stones, others using their teeth as mortars;
some subsisted on withered leaves, others had water as their food,
and others, subsisting on air, practiced most dreadful austerity.

The brahmins said:
'We shall not go back to Camatkārapura.
There are other brahmins there, masters of the Vedas and their auxiliary sciences;
